    <string name="katha">Story</string>
    <string name="katha_title">The story of Ram Setu</string>
    <string name="katha_body">In the Ramayana, when Lord Rama needed to reach Lanka to free Sita from Ravana, the vanara army had to build a bridge across the sea.\n\nNala and Nila had a boon that stones they touched would float. The army wrote Rama\'s name on each stone and set them on the water. By his grace the stones did not sink, and the hundred-yojana Ram Setu was born.</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_title">How to play:</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_body">• Tap floating stones near the gold line.\n• Catch a stone on the line for a Perfect hit.\n• Do not let any stone sink into the deep.\n• The bridge speeds up as your collection grows.</string>
    <string name="katha_close">Jai Shri Ram</string>
